=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  logforward review-journald -----------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Decided: no Figma frame. journald's Set server: rsyslog is$
# installed first, and the notice says what else that does.$
$
  Checking the host...$
$
# Set server ###################################################$
$
# Note$
# rsyslog is installed to forward the journal. It also keeps its$
# own log files under /var/log.$
$
  Forwarding ---------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Server               192.0.2.50:514$
   -  Protocol             TCP not encrypted$
$
   -  Install rsyslog$
      rsyslog$
      -not installed$
      +installed$
      $ apt-get install -y rsyslog$
$
   -  Write hardn's forwarding file$
      /etc/rsyslog.d/60-hardn-forward.conf$
      @@ -0,0 +1,4 @@$
      +# Written by hardn (Log Forwarding).$
      +*.* action(type="omfwd" protocol="tcp"$
      +    target="192.0.2.50" port="514"$
      +    queue.type="linkedList")$
      $ rsyslogd -N1$
$
   -  Restart rsyslog$
      rsyslog$
      $ systemctl restart rsyslog$
$
   -  Send a test line$
      $ logger -t hardn "log forwarding set"$
$
  Forward logs to 192.0.2.50? [y/N, 0 or q]: $
$
$

